# Reference only. The easy way to fill these in is:
#
#   pwsh ./scripts/set-keys.ps1     (or ./scripts/set-keys.sh)
#
# which prompts with the typing hidden, checks .env.local really is ignored
# before writing a secret to it, and upserts — so changing one value leaves the
# others alone.
#
# If you would rather edit by hand: copy this to .env.local and fill it in.
# .env.local is gitignored; this example is not, so never put a real value here.
#
# The npm scripts load .env.local with node --env-file-if-exists, so once it is
# here nothing needs exporting and nothing needs passing on the command line.

# Google AI Studio, for scripts/sourcing/scan.mjs — the stage that writes each
# lead's observation. Free, no card: aistudio.google.com/apikey
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Rate limits are NOT set here. They are per model, not per account, and live
# in scripts/sourcing/gemini.mjs — Flash-Lite's 1,000 requests a day and Flash's
# 250 are separate budgets. A 429 is believed over that table and the observed
# ceiling is recorded, so the numbers being slightly stale costs one wasted
# request rather than a wrong answer.

# Companies House REST API, for scripts/sourcing/pull.mjs — the lead puller.
# Free: developer.company-information.service.gov.uk → Your applications →
# Create an application (Live, not Test) → Add a new key → REST. Leave the IP
# restriction off. 600 requests per five minutes, which pull.mjs paces itself to.
COMPANIES_HOUSE_API_KEY=

# A SECOND Google AI Studio project's key, for the puller's prospector only
# (npm run sourcing:pull -- --judge). Deliberately not GEMINI_API_KEY: quota is
# per project, and prospecting on the writer's key would stop the writer —
# which one key alone did before eleven in the morning on 16 September. The
# puller refuses to fall back to GEMINI_API_KEY rather than do that silently.
GEMINI_DISCOVERY_API_KEY=

# Google Search Console ownership token, for the site build. Search Console →
# add property → HTML tag, then copy just the content value out of the tag.
GSC_VERIFICATION=
